## Lore

Iktektumiks, called Ikteks or Diggers, come from a gigantic desert world
belonging to a long-absent god, where they are the smallest creatures
around and prey to nearly everything. On Rifts Earth they stand seven to
nine and a half feet tall: digitigrade, thick-legged, long-armed, with pale
yellow to rusty red skin like fine pebbles, wide-set eyes either side of a
broad flat nose, and tall pointed ears like a horse''s.

Life on the run made them diggers, trappers and survivors, with keen senses
and a few instinctive psychic tricks for spotting danger. Their home world
never let them settle long enough to build a society, and they arrive
through random Rifts, mostly into the New West, as a Stone Age people with
no written language. Earth gives them their first real chance. They are
quick thinkers and eager learners; some cling to spears, hide armor and
digging tools, while others take to Vibro-Blades, energy rifles, trucks
and hovercycles. Many are only now realizing that, here, they are no longer
the prey.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an optional player character or NPC.

Also called Tunnelers, Desert Savages and Horse-legged Diggers.

Size 7 to 9.6 feet (2.1 to 2.9 m). Weight 250 to 400 pounds (112.5 to 180
kg). Life span 4D6+34 years; mature by 16; one or two young after a 22
month gestation. Slave market value about double a human''s.

Ikteks who keep the old ways avoid cybernetics; others take implants as
readily as anyone, though their size makes parts hard to find. Common
magic paths are Elemental Fusionist, Warlock, Witch, Priest and Mystic, or
Shaman and Totem Warrior among the traditionalists.

Habitat: the New West from old Canada to northern Mexico, favoring hot
country such as Utah, Nevada, Arizona and New Mexico.

Allies: Native American tribes, Psi-Stalkers, Simvan, nomads, Cactus People,
Fennodi and other peaceful peoples. Enemies: they dislike bullies, and
sometimes clash with other nomads over territory, usually backing down.
